    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.09_minimal_category_theory.chapters.01_objects_and_arrows.sections.04_concrete_anchor_survey.concrete_anchor_7_DMittens#d_mittens" .
silm:instances_papers_09_minimal_category_theory_chapters_01_objects_and_arrows_sections_04_concrete_anchor_survey_concrete_anchor_7_DMittens#d_mittens silm:hasLongDescription "The D_Mittens is the source diagram indexing the eleven typed source legs of the Mittens colimit problem (record, identifier, quality, measurement, value, unit, role, process, taxon, validation, witness). In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'D_Mittens', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
